#: ../../source/docs/weathervaning.rst:4
#: 499928b671e346f6b469df627ad75671
msgid "Weathervaning and Wind Hold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/weathervaning.rst:6
#: dfe72c40b37a484ba05f1507f2684e00
msgid "Flying a Traditional Helicopter, or some Multicopters, in significant levels of wind can present a challenge. The issue is that any flat plate surface, such as a Traditional Helicopter's tail fin and boom, offers a lot of surface area for the wind to interact with. That can lead to a reduction in attitude and position control and high motor and ESC load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/weathervaning.rst:11
#: 312c4652dd384090a02dd81c0f57dfeb
msgid "To reduce the impact of wind when flying in VTOL modes the ArduPilot code supports active yaw axis weathervaning which can greatly reduce the impact of wind on VTOL flight by keeping the vehicle pointed into the wind and reducing the surface area exposed to the wind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/weathervaning.rst:16
#: d5f9a6d4d59d484bb6675d650bc3fd26
msgid "Active Weathervaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/weathervaning.rst:18
#: cc24240ebbac43d681fa1272fa32ae70
msgid "Active weathervaning acts to turn the aircraft into the wind when flying in GUIDED and/or AUTO modes. You can enable active weathervaning by setting the :ref:`WVANE_ENABLE <WVANE_ENABLE>` parameter to a non-zero value and selecting to use it in either GUIDED and/or AUTO modes. The default is not to use active weathervaning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/weathervaning.rst:24
#: c8e88c8ca8964f6e826b3e9c7b09409d
msgid ":ref:`WVANE_ENABLE<WVANE_ENABLE>` Value"
msgstr ""

